Lastly, ensuring explicability in AI recommendations could involve maintaining detailed logs of AI decision-making processes and providing clear, understandable explanations of how these decisions are reached, though specific measures for achieving this are not detailed in the provided context. Regular security audits, including annual penetration testing and post-major release testing, help identify vulnerabilities early on.

In summary, while several necessary measures are already in place or planned, such as data residency within the EU, anonymization tools, AI security controls, and GDPR compliance mechanisms, ensuring encryption of sensitive data and enhancing explicability and transparency for AI recommendations are key areas to focus on. Implementing these requirements will help ensure that the solution meets all specified security and regulatory demands.
